    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/46119": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Dental Medicine",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Dental Medicine Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Assistant Professor of Dental Medicine Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Dental Medicine Department College of Dental Medicine Position Category Faculty Job Description The Preclinical Assistant Professor of Dental Medicine is responsible for the instruction and supervision of dental students in simulation and laboratory settings. This role supports the foundational training of students in operative dentistry, fixed and removable prosthodontics, dental anatomy, and other essential preclinical skills. The instructor ensures that students gain proficiency in hand skills, critical thinking, and adherence to professional and academic standards, preparing them for entry into the clinical phase of their education Required Qualifications DDS , DMD , or equivalent dental degree from an accredited institution. Proficiency in basic and advanced restorative dental procedures. Eligibility for dental licensure or faculty permit in the state of employment strongly preferred Commitment to excellence in teaching, student mentorship, and preclinical education Preferred Qualifications Prior teaching experience in a dental academic setting or simulation laboratory. Familiarity with preclinical grading rubrics and assessment tools. Experience with digital dentistry, CAD / CAM , or virtual simulation technologies. Commitment to fostering an inclusive, student-centered learning environment. Physical Demands Campus LMU Tower Job Duty Job Duty Teach and demonstrate preclinical procedures in simulation labs, including but not limited to operative dentistry, dental anatomy, occlusion, and prosthodontics Job Duty Provide individualized and small-group instruction to guide students through lab exercises and projects Job Duty Reinforce principles taught in didactic courses through hands-on application Job Duty Evaluate student work using established rubrics and performance criteria Job Duty Provide timely, constructive feedback to support skill development and continuous improvement Job Duty Assist with practical examinations, skill checks, and competency assessments Job Duty Ensure lab equipment, instruments, and materials are prepared and maintained for instructional use Job Duty Monitor student adherence to infection control and safety protocols within the lab. Job Duty Model professionalism, ethical behavior, and teamwork in all interactions with students and colleagues Job Duty Serve as a mentor to students by supporting their academic and professional development Job Duty Work collaboratively with course directors, faculty, and lab staff to support course objectives and student success Job Duty Participate in faculty meetings, calibration sessions, and departmental planning activities Job Duty Provide input on curriculum development and continuous improvement of preclinical courses Job Duty Contribute to the development and revision of instructional materials and lab manuals Job Duty Support an inclusive and respectful learning environment where all students feel welcome and empowered to succeed Job Duty Demonstrate sensitivity to diverse student needs and learning styles Job Duty Perform additional responsibilities as requested by department chairs or course directors to support the mission and operations of the dental school Posting Detail Information Posting Number F01330P Job Open Date 07/23/2026 Job Close Date 12/31/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/37093 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter Transcripts To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
