      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Director of LMU Clinical DVM Program Operations &amp; Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Director of LMU Clinical DVM Program Operations & Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Director of LMU Clinical DVM Program Operations & Assistant Professor Department CVM Clinical Relations Position Category Faculty Job Description The Director of LMU Clinical DVM Program Operations, in collaboration with the Executive Associate Dean of Clinical Relations and Outreach, and other Clinical Relations and Outreach faculty and staff, provides operational and executional expertise to the LMU Clinical DVM Program. The position will have input on shaping the LMU Clinical DVM program and educating future veterinarians. The position will be remote and will require occasional travel to LMU DVM instructional sites. Required Qualifications DVM Preferred Qualifications MBA or board certification; at least 10 years in clinical practice or academia Physical Demands Campus Remote Job Duty Job Duty Manage the LMU DVM Clinical Course Mentor Program Job Duty Manage the LMU DVM Clinical Site Training Program Job Duty Manage the LMU DVM Clinical Year Student Success Program Job Duty Manage the LMU DVM Professional Quality Assurance Program Job Duty Promote the mission of Lincoln Memorial University to all faculty, staff, students, and the community at large Job Duty Work closely and collaboratively with the Executive Associate Dean of Clinical Relations and Outreach. Job Duty Collaborate and foster working relationships with students, staff, peer faculty, other colleges on campus, and external partners and stakeholders to attain the college’s and University’s goals and objectives. Job Duty Engage in service to the college and beyond, develop and deliver instructional materials, and perform research based on assigned full-time equivalent Job Duty Provide oversight for implementation of initiatives and the strengthening and fulfillment of the college mission. Job Duty Assure student learning outcomes are achieved and measurable, using both qualitative and quantitative metrics, within the hybrid distributed clinical education model. Job Duty Participate in regularly scheduled meetings of personnel assigned to the Clinical Relations and Outreach team Job Duty Prepare required reports Job Duty Assure that the college is represented at appropriate AAVMC , AVMA , State VMA , and other professional programs, initiatives, and events as designated Job Duty Effectively deliver presentations to students, clinical affiliates, and other parties Job Duty Travel periodically as needed. Job Duty Participate in other strategic initiatives as assigned Posting Detail Information Posting Number F01832P Job Open Date 09/03/2026 Job Close Date 12/18/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University p