    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/46009": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Social Work &amp; Field Coordinator",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Social Work &amp; Field Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Assistant Professor of Social Work & Field Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Social Work & Field Coordinator Department SOCIAL WORK Position Category Faculty Job Description The instructional faculty member/Social Work Field Coordinator shall have the primary responsibilities of teaching, research/creative achievement, and service functions (including serving as the Field Coordinator) and shall be held accountable for these obligations as they contribute to the attainment of the mission of the University, the School, the Department, and the Program. Required Qualifications MSW from a Council on Social Work Education ( CSWE ) accreditied program; at least two years of practice experience in service delivery settings; *educational preparation in accordance with requirements of the University and the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools; *evidence of potential for effective undergraduate teaching and scholarly activity; *licensed or license eligible in Tennessee *potential for operating in the field and servicing interns and externs as needed. Preferred Qualifications PhD or DSW in Social Work Physical Demands Campus Harrogate Job Duty Job Duty promote the mission of Lincoln Memorial University to all faculty, staff, students and to the community at large; Job Duty promote effective working relationships among faculty, staff and students; Job Duty participate on department, school, and university committees; Job Duty comply with the university Faculty/Staff Policy Manual in instructional and other requirements; Job Duty administer, develop, implement, monitor, and evaluate the field and internship seminars, placements, and student experiences of the Social Work Program within the guidelines of the Program, the Department, the School, the University, the Council on Social Work Education ( CSWE ), and the National Association of Social Workers ( NASW ); Job Duty participate in recruitment, community, and public service opportunities; Job Duty complete required institutional and program accreditation reports and other reports necessary for the operation and advancement of the University; and Job Duty appropriately align course syllabi goals and objectives to academic major program goals and student outcomes for each course taught; Job Duty develop a current syllabus for each assigned class and distribute a course syllabus to each student Job Duty submit a current copy of each syllabus to the Social Work department chair by a predetermined deadline Job Duty evaluate enrolled students and submit grades to the Registrar by a predetermined deadline; Job Duty participate in the faculty evaluation process and use the results to improve teaching and strengthen the major; Job Duty attend department, school, convocation, and university faculty meetings Job Duty perform other duties as assigned. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F01838P Job Open Date 09/08/2026 Job Close Date 01/08/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination