    "https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/45225": {
      "title": "Principal Faculty - Pharmacology - Tampa PA Program",
      "description": "Lincoln Memorial University Applicant Portal | Principal Faculty - Pharmacology - Tampa PA Program Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) LMU Annual Security Availability Know Your Rights Principal Faculty - Pharmacology - Tampa PA Program Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Principal Faculty - Pharmacology - Tampa PA Program Department PA Program Tampa Position Category Faculty Job Description Under the direction of the Program Director, the primary responsibilities of the Principal Faculty are to design, implement, coordinate, and evaluate the Didactic Phase curriculum. * Additionally, the fulfillment of the following LMU - SMS faculty duties Provide student instruction Evaluate student performance*Provide academic counseling for students*Assure the availability of remedial instruction Select student applicants for admission to the Program*Evaluate the Program*Participate in Program/ SMS / LMU committees*Complete scholarly activities Required Qualifications Graduation from an accredited school of pharmacy with a doctoral degree is required. A minimum of 2 years of full-time clinical experience as a licensed pharmacist. ? Current Florida licensure as a pharmacist or eligibility to obtain licensure. Excellent oral, written, organizational, and computer skills. Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching experience in a Physician Assistant or other health profession program is preferred. Physical Demands Campus Brandon Florida Job Duty Job Duty Serve as Course Director for Pharmacology courses Job Duty Design and revise course syllabi Job Duty Provide guidance to Principal Faculty and Instructional Faculty on the following Job Duty Course learning outcomes and instructional objectives Job Duty Depth and breadth of content to be covered Job Duty Format of instruction delivery Job Duty Update course content to reflect new FDA drug approvals, black-box warnings, and shifts in clinical practice guidelines (e.g., ADA , ACC / AHA ). Job Duty Develop and validate assessments that specifically measure clinical reasoning in pharmacotherapy and safe prescribing habits Job Duty Format of assessment of student performance Job Duty Complete End-of-Course reports for assigned Didactic Phase courses and present conclusions based on data analysis and recommendations for action(s)/modification(s) to the Curriculum Committee Job Duty Participate in the design, implementation, coordination, and evaluation of the Didactic Cumulative Assessment and the Summative Evaluation Job Duty Serve as the primary liaison for interprofessional education ( IPE ) initiatives between the PA program and other medical/pharmacy disciplines Job Duty Provide academic counseling for students enrolled in the Program Job Duty Assist in the review/revision of the Student Handbook and the Student Catalog as assigned. Job Duty Participate in the Program’s continuous self-assessment process as directed Job Duty Assist the Program Director in preparing documentation for the Accreditation Review Commission on the Education of the Physician Assistant, Inc. ( ARC -PA) and the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools, Commission on Colleges ( SACSCOC ) as requested. Job Duty Adhere to all Program, SMS , and LMU policies and procedures Job Duty Promote a positive learning environment for all students Job Duty Provide instruction in pharmacology for students in a variety of formats for Didactic Phase courses Job Duty Assess student performance in a variety of assessments in the Didactic Phase. Job Duty Provide remedial instruction for students identified to be at-risk or requiring remediation in the Didactic Phase Job Duty Assess student performance in the Didactic Phase and student readiness to progress to the Clinical Phase Job Duty Assess student performance in the Clinical Phase Cumulative Assessment and student readiness to progress to the Summative Evaluation. Job Duty Assess student performance in the Summative Evaluation and student readiness to progress to Graduation. Job Duty Participate in Program committees as assigned (Faculty Staff Committee, Curriculum Committee, Admissions Committee, and Student Progress Committee) Job Duty Participate in SMS and LMU committees as assigned. Job Duty Participate in the development, review, and revision of the Program’s mission statement, goals, learning outcomes, and graduate competencies Job Duty Participate in the selection of student applicants for admission to the Program. Stay current with clinical practice standards through active clinical practice and/or pursuit of continuing education Job Duty Stay current with standards of PA education through pursuit of continuing education (e.g. conferences, seminars, workshops, community groups, etc.) Job Duty Consider scholarship opportunities such as participating in original research, peer-reviewed publications, presentations at professional conferences, and collaboration with colleagues and other health professionals. Job Duty Promote the mission of LMU , the SMS , and the Program to all faculty, staff, students, and members of the community. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F01662P Job Open Date 05/07/2026 Job Close Date 10/31/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary About the Institution Lincoln Memorial University is a values-based learning community dedicated to providing educational experiences in the liberal arts and professional studies. The main campus is located in Harrogate, Tennessee. For more information about employment opportunities, contact the Office of Human Resources at 423-869-7112 or humanresources@lmunet.edu . AA/EEO Statement Lincoln Memorial University is an Equal Opportunity education institution. Lincoln Memorial University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, veteran status, military status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in all University programs and activities. Background Check Statement The University will conduct criminal background checks on all employees. Background checks may include but are not limited to confirmation of the individual’s identity, credit information, motor vehicle driving record, review of an individual’s criminal conviction record (if any), verification of any license, and certificate or degree required for the position. Quicklink for Posting https://careers.lmunet.edu/postings/42807 Minimum Salary Maximum Salary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter Transcripts To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
